{"id":"u-023bc66d-15bb-4800-a2d8-13359eedd10b","src":"community","title":"Kratos | Physique and Strength of the God of War","author":"Hadrian","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/m5EMgZ-kratos-or-physique-and-strength-of-the-god-of-war","desc":"“Kratos” is built to forge a strong, muscular upper body through a combination of strength training and hypertrophy work. Each session is made to grow size where it counts. Chest, delts, arms, and back will all be hammered, (legs will still be a part of the program) while developing the raw strength to prove it. It’s not just about looking like a god-slayer, but having the strength of one.\n———————————\nThe ideal way to run “Kratos” is to do all three blocks, although, you can choose to run singular blocks instead.\n\nBlock 1 - Block 1 takes a both hypertrophy and strength-based approach. This is the main block of the program that defines mass and strength put together into one block.\n\nBlock 2 - Block 2 focuses on more of a hypertrophy progression, while having it’s main focus put towards mass. The muscular growth from this block should be the most significant.\n\nBlock 3 - Block 3 focuses on more of a strength progression, while still having it’s hypertrophy elements. The strength gains from this block should be the most significant.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Beginner"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Women's","Bodyweight Fitness","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":50,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-07T00:45:19.819Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chaos - Chest (Block 1)","Jörgmungandr - Back (Block 1)","Spartan Rage - Arms and Core","Yggdrasil - Legs (Block 1)","Atlas - Shoulders (Block 1)","Bladed Exile - Arms and Core"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"x":3},{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi